eval/README.md:`stub/n/<case-id>.json` contains each editable canned answer. Change a location, resolution, count, limit, or fake label and rerun: the evaluator should report NOT MET. Identical commands have identical canned files; the stub rejects disagreement among them, so changing any one is observable. Unknown commands print the empty static-analysis answer required by the brief.
eval/README.md:These checks were written by P2 Codex independently of the future builder. Passing the stub validates evaluator plumbing and its known n. It does not establish correctness of a future tool on other source projects.
eval/README.md:The generator leaves filenames stable, inserts seed-chosen blank/comment lines in every source file and blank lines in every tsconfig, and renames declared identifiers and their references, including contextual identifier names such as `assert`. Each name uses a seed-specific suffix; same-spelled members stay same-spelled so the type-versus-name fixture remains adversarial. Source literals, titles, import paths and external built-in names stay intact. Property accesses are checked against TypeScript declaration files so a local parameter named `value` does not rename the iterator result’s built-in `.value` member. Root and project paths in the generated case file are absolute. Location expectations, queries, names and source text expectations are rewritten from the original source's line/name maps. The generator never reads canned n; tests transform canned witnesses to validate the resulting cases against the written source. The bundled stub's exact argument lookup intentionally fails on a held-out root.
eval/COVERAGE.md:Checker author: P2 Codex. The acceptance and mutation checks below were written by the evaluator's author. They test the evaluator and canned fixture n, not the future builder's correctness on real repositories.
eval/COVERAGE.md:evaluator and its canned n, not an independent implementation or correctness on opencode.
